---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import JsonLd from '~/components/common/JsonLd.astro';

const metadata = {
  title: 'PVC vs Hypalon Inflatable Boats –Which Material Is Better?',
  description:
    'Compare PVC and Hypalon (CSM) inflatable boat materials across durability, weight, UV resistance, repairability, cost, and best use cases. Make an informed purchasing decision.',
  ignoreTitleTemplate: true,
};
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>
  <JsonLd
    type="Article"
    article={{
      headline: 'PVC vs Hypalon Inflatable Boats –Which Material Is Better?',
      description:
        'Compare PVC and Hypalon (CSM) inflatable boat materials across durability, weight, UV resistance, repairability, cost, and best use cases.',
      datePublished: '2026-07-27',
    }}
    data={{ url: 'https://afarer.com/compare/pvc-vs-hypalon' }}
  />
  <JsonLd
    type="BreadcrumbList"
    breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Compare', href: '/compare' }, { name: 'PVC vs Hypalon' }]}
  />
  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto py-24 px-6">
    <a href="/compare" class="text-sm text-sky-600 hover:text-sky-700">&larr; All Comparisons</a>
    <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-semibold text-gray-900">PVC vs Hypalon Inflatable Boats</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-gray-500">
      Choosing between PVC and Hypalon (CSM) for your inflatable boat is one of the most important material decisions
      you will make. Here is everything you need to know.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-12 overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b-2 border-gray-200">
            <th class="text-left py-4 px-4 font-semibold text-gray-900">Factor</th>
            <th class="text-left py-4 px-4 font-semibold text-sky-700 bg-sky-50">PVC (Military-Grade)</th>
            <th class="text-left py-4 px-4 font-semibold text-emerald-700 bg-emerald-50">Hypalon (CSM)</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-100">
          <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50"
            ><td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-gray-900">Durability</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600"
              >Excellent for recreational use. Resists punctures and abrasion.</td
            ><td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600">Superior. Withstands extreme abrasion, chemicals, and heat.</td></tr
          >
          <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50"
            ><td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-gray-900">UV Resistance</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600"
              >Good with UV-resistant coating. Degrades faster without protection.</td
            ><td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600">Excellent. Natural resistance to UV, ozone, and weathering.</td></tr
          >
          <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50"
            ><td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-gray-900">Weight</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600"
              >Lighter. Easier to carry, pack, and inflate manually.</td
            ><td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600">Heavier. Requires more effort to transport and inflate.</td></tr
          >
          <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50"
            ><td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-gray-900">Repairability</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600"
              >Easy. PVC patches bond quickly with standard adhesive.</td
            ><td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600">Moderate. Requires Hypalon-specific adhesive and more curing time.</td
            ></tr
          >
          <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50"
            ><td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-gray-900">Cost</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600"
              >More affordable. Best value for recreational boaters.</td
            ><td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600">More expensive. 30-50% higher than equivalent PVC models.</td></tr
          >
          <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50"
            ><td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-gray-900">Lifespan</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600"
              >5-10 years with proper care and storage.</td
            ><td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600">10-15+ years. Longer lifespan under sustained UV exposure.</td></tr
          >
          <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50"
            ><td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-gray-900">Flexibility in Cold</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600"
              >Stiffens in cold weather. Avoid below -10°C.</td
            ><td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600">Remains flexible in extreme cold. Preferred for arctic conditions.</td
            ></tr
          >
          <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50"
            ><td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-gray-900">Chemical Resistance</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600"
              >Moderate. Avoid fuel and oil contact.</td
            ><td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600">Excellent. Resists fuel, oil, and most chemicals.</td></tr
          >
          <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50"
            ><td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-gray-900">Best For</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600"
              >Recreational boating, SUP, family use, rental fleets.</td
            ><td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-600">Commercial, military, rescue, expedition, extreme environments.</td
            ></tr
          >
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900">When to Choose PVC</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
      Military-grade triple-layer PVC — as used in all afarer recreational boats — offers the best balance of weight,
      durability, and cost for most boaters. If you use your boat on weekends, store it properly, and want the best
      value, PVC is the right choice. Modern PVC formulations with UV-resistant coatings have closed the gap with
      Hypalon for recreational use.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900">When to Choose Hypalon</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
      Hypalon (CSM) is the professional choice for commercial operators, military, search and rescue, and expeditions in
      extreme environments. If your boat stays inflated for months at a time in tropical sun, operates in chemically
      aggressive environments (fuel docks, industrial waterways), or needs to perform reliably in arctic conditions,
      Hypalon's premium cost is justified.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900">The Bottom Line</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
      For 90% of recreational boaters, military-grade PVC delivers the best value. For professional/commercial operators
      who need maximum durability in harsh conditions, Hypalon is the superior investment. Afarer offers both material
      options across our product lines — contact our team for guidance on your specific use case.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
